hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"934","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’, Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman, Ali bin Khashram, and Ahmad bin Abdah told us, they said: Sufyan told us, Abdul Jabbar said, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, he heard Anas bin Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and others said on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If dinner is prepared and the prayer is established, then start with dinner.” Al-Makhzoumi also said: Anas bin Malik heard"
"935","Imran bin Musa Al-Qazzaz told us, Abdul-Warith told us, Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “When dinner is served and prayer is called, start with dinner.” He said: Ibn Umar had dinner one night while he was listening to the imam’s reading."
